node_modules/
dist/

# Real environment config — never commit it. Covers variants like .env.production
# too; .env.example is the template that stays in the repo.
.env*
!.env.example

# The database — never commit real data. data/ is where it lives by default (and
# where Docker mounts it), so the whole folder is ignored: the database, its
# WAL/journal files, backups, and Litestream's replication files. The leading
# slash limits this to the top-level data/ — without it, scripts/data/ (the seed
# files, which must be committed) would be ignored too. The patterns after it
# catch a SQLite database put anywhere else (and Windows' Thumbs.db).
/data/
*.db
*.db-*
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

*.log
.DS_Store
